# Context Engine — Kiro Memory Rules

## ON EVERY NEW CHAT: Call gather_context() first
This project uses Context Engine for persistent memory. At the start of every new chat
or after a context window reset, call gather_context() via MCP BEFORE responding.
The context engine DB (context.db) is the source of truth — not your context window.

## COMMIT STRUCTURE (mandatory format)
topic: "[Category] Short title"
  Categories: [Bug Fix] [Feature] [Config] [Design] [API] [Refactor] [Decision]
summary: What was done and why (1-3 sentences, specific enough to reconstruct)
kept_refs: Exact code snippets, paths, and values — NOT descriptions

## WHEN TO COMMIT
Commit after: bug fixes, features, confirmed configs, API shapes, architectural decisions.
Do NOT commit: during work-in-progress, for questions, or casual chat.

## CLI COMMANDS
  context-engine status    → session/branch/token stats
  context-engine log       → commit history
  context-engine branches  → list branches
  context-engine sessions  → list all projects
